Fixes #97055 (residual cache-identity gap)

AI-assisted: this PR was prepared with Codex and reviewed with Claude.

## What Problem This Solves

The core misrouting from #97055 — custom Ollama memory providers (`ollama-cpu`, `ollama-gpu`, …) being collapsed onto the default `ollama` provider — has already landed on `main` via fa5f24b021e (adapter-side provider-id resolution) and b085184d085 (gateway-side provider-id propagation). This PR has been slimmed down to the remaining gap: the Ollama memory adapter's embedding cache identity is still only `{provider, model, outputDimensionality}`. Two configurations that reuse the same provider id but point at different endpoints (different `baseUrl`, or different non-secret custom headers selecting a different tenant/backend) hash to the same memory provider key and silently reuse stale cached embeddings from the other endpoint.

## Why This Change Was Made

The lmstudio memory adapter already keys its cache by `{provider, baseUrl, model, headers: sanitizeEmbeddingCacheHeaders(...)}`; the Ollama adapter now mirrors that pattern exactly (keeping its existing `outputDimensionality` field), so endpoint identity participates in the cache key consistently across local-server adapters.

**Secret-header hardening:** because `cacheKeyData` is hashed into the memory provider key, a credential header in it would force a full reindex on every credential rotation. `sanitizeEmbeddingCacheHeaders` in `memory-host-sdk` now always drops sensitive header names (`authorization`, `proxy-authorization`, and anything containing `api-key`/`token`/`secret`) for every adapter, and `excludedHeaderNames` becomes optional. Secret headers are still sent on the wire — only the cache identity excludes them.

## User Impact

- Users running multiple Ollama endpoints under distinct provider ids (or re-pointing one id at a new `baseUrl`) get correct, endpoint-scoped embedding caches instead of silent stale reuse.
- Rotating a credential header no longer churns the memory index, for any embedding adapter.
- **Compatibility note (maintainer acceptance item):** adding `baseUrl`/`headers` to the Ollama cache identity changes the provider-key hash for existing Ollama memory indexes (including the default `ollama` provider), so they rebuild once via the normal memory index rebuild flow on upgrade. This is intentional — it is required to distinguish endpoints, and memory indexes are rebuildable.

## Evidence

### Real-behavior proof — the exact provider cache key memory-core persists

This drives the **real** `ollamaMemoryEmbeddingProviderAdapter.create()` for ONE provider id (`ollama`) against two different endpoints, then computes the exact key memory-core writes as the index provider identity: `hashText(JSON.stringify(cacheKeyData))` (`extensions/memory-core/src/memory/manager-reindex-state.ts:55`). No mocks — real adapter, real hash.

**Before — `origin/main` @ `e43bd3d57bc`** (both endpoints collide on one key → the second endpoint silently reuses the first's cached embeddings):
```
======== REAL ollama memory embedding cache identity ========
provider id (both): ollama    model (both): nomic-embed-text

endpoint A  baseUrl=http://127.0.0.1:11434
  cacheKeyData = {"provider":"ollama","model":"nomic-embed-text"}
  providerKey  = 0eeec5c660cc1b0f3d2b83e8f758d4c80fba365db6ec183b4679534368c78085

endpoint B  baseUrl=http://10.0.0.5:11434
  cacheKeyData = {"provider":"ollama","model":"nomic-embed-text"}
  providerKey  = 0eeec5c660cc1b0f3d2b83e8f758d4c80fba365db6ec183b4679534368c78085

A vs B providerKey differ:            false
```

**After — this branch @ `850ea819308`** (each endpoint gets its own key → a change reindexes; the secret `authorization` header is stripped from the identity so rotating it does not churn the index):
```
======== REAL ollama memory embedding cache identity ========
provider id (both): ollama    model (both): nomic-embed-text

endpoint A  baseUrl=http://127.0.0.1:11434
  cacheKeyData = {"provider":"ollama","baseUrl":"http://127.0.0.1:11434","model":"nomic-embed-text","headers":[["Content-Type","application/json"]]}
  providerKey  = 780c71a6cdf63a0d574b4baf77afbf734b7bf3abf3253e177a9654a0658eb7a1

endpoint B  baseUrl=http://10.0.0.5:11434
  cacheKeyData = {"provider":"ollama","baseUrl":"http://10.0.0.5:11434","model":"nomic-embed-text","headers":[["Content-Type","application/json"]]}
  providerKey  = cd5a7580e8a73582a364a1100623226284f32e4bb8a409fae29f6887ab9919cb

endpoint A + secret authorization header
  cacheKeyData = {"provider":"ollama","baseUrl":"http://127.0.0.1:11434","model":"nomic-embed-text","headers":[["Content-Type","application/json"]]}
  providerKey  = 780c71a6cdf63a0d574b4baf77afbf734b7bf3abf3253e177a9654a0658eb7a1

A vs B providerKey differ:            true
secret token absent from cache data:  true
```

The harness asserts the two endpoints' persisted keys differ and that no secret token appears in the cache identity; it passes on this branch and fails on main (`AssertionError: expected '0eeec5c6…' not to be '0eeec5c6…'`).

<details><summary>Reproduce (drop into <code>extensions/ollama/src/</code> and <code>pnpm test</code> it on either checkout)</summary>

```ts
// Real-behavior proof for issue #97055 / PR #97059 (residual cache-identity gap).
// Drives the REAL ollama memory embedding adapter `create()` for ONE provider id
// ("ollama") against two different endpoints, then computes the EXACT provider
// cache key memory-core persists — `hashText(JSON.stringify(cacheKeyData))`
// (extensions/memory-core/src/memory/manager-reindex-state.ts:55). On this branch
// the two endpoints yield different keys (endpoint change -> reindex); on main
// they collide (endpoint change -> silent stale embedding reuse). Run:
//   pnpm test extensions/ollama/src/memory-cache-identity.proof.test.ts
import fs from "node:fs/promises";
import os from "node:os";
import path from "node:path";
import type { OpenClawConfig } from "openclaw/plugin-sdk";
import { hashText } from "openclaw/plugin-sdk/memory-core-host-engine-storage";
import { expect, it } from "vitest";
import { ollamaMemoryEmbeddingProviderAdapter as adapter } from "./memory-embedding-adapter.js";

async function providerKeyFor(remote: {
  baseUrl: string;
  headers?: Record<string, string>;
}): Promise<{ cacheKeyData: Record<string, unknown>; providerKey: string }> {
  const created = await adapter.create({
    config: {} as OpenClawConfig,
    provider: "ollama", // SAME provider id for both endpoints
    model: "nomic-embed-text",
    remote,
  } as Parameters<typeof adapter.create>[0]);
  const cacheKeyData = (created.runtime.cacheKeyData ?? {}) as Record<string, unknown>;
  // Exact key memory-core writes as the index provider identity.
  const providerKey = hashText(JSON.stringify(cacheKeyData));
  return { cacheKeyData, providerKey };
}

it("PROOF #97055: same provider id, different endpoints -> distinct memory cache keys", async () => {
  const endpointA = await providerKeyFor({ baseUrl: "http://127.0.0.1:11434" });
  const endpointB = await providerKeyFor({ baseUrl: "http://10.0.0.5:11434" });
  const secretHeader = await providerKeyFor({
    baseUrl: "http://127.0.0.1:11434",
    headers: { authorization: "Bearer super-secret-token" },
  });

  const transcript = [
    "======== REAL ollama memory embedding cache identity ========",
    "provider id (both): ollama    model (both): nomic-embed-text",
    "",
    `endpoint A  baseUrl=http://127.0.0.1:11434`,
    `  cacheKeyData = ${JSON.stringify(endpointA.cacheKeyData)}`,
    `  providerKey  = ${endpointA.providerKey}`,
    "",
    `endpoint B  baseUrl=http://10.0.0.5:11434`,
    `  cacheKeyData = ${JSON.stringify(endpointB.cacheKeyData)}`,
    `  providerKey  = ${endpointB.providerKey}`,
    "",
    `endpoint A + secret authorization header`,
    `  cacheKeyData = ${JSON.stringify(secretHeader.cacheKeyData)}`,
    `  providerKey  = ${secretHeader.providerKey}`,
    "",
    `A vs B providerKey differ:            ${endpointA.providerKey !== endpointB.providerKey}`,
    `secret token absent from cache data:  ${!JSON.stringify(secretHeader.cacheKeyData).includes("super-secret-token")}`,
    "=============================================================",
  ].join("\n");
  await fs.writeFile(path.join(os.tmpdir(), "proof-97055-out.txt"), transcript, "utf8");

  // Endpoint change under one provider id must change the persisted key
  // (so memory-core reindexes instead of reusing the other endpoint's cache).
  expect(endpointA.providerKey).not.toBe(endpointB.providerKey);
  // Secret headers are never baked into the cache identity.
  expect(JSON.stringify(secretHeader.cacheKeyData)).not.toContain("super-secret-token");
});
```
</details>

### Notes

The provider-id **routing** fix for #97055 already landed on `main` (fa5f24b021e, b085184d085) and is covered by main's own tests; this PR is the residual **cache-identity** parity, mirroring the lmstudio adapter. `pnpm tsgo:core` and `pnpm tsgo:extensions` are clean.

**Compatibility (maintainer acceptance item):** adding `baseUrl`/`headers` to the Ollama cache identity changes the provider-key hash for existing Ollama memory indexes, so they rebuild once via the normal memory index rebuild flow on upgrade. Intentional and required to distinguish endpoints; memory indexes are rebuildable.

